      ":question/problem": "What is the coefficient matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{1} &=3{x}_{3} \\\\ -11{x}_{3} &=12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}-11{x}_{3} &=12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
